{"uid":"modules/loop_preflight.py","name":"loop_preflight.py","qualname":"modules/loop_preflight.py","kind":"module","file":"modules/loop_preflight.py","line":1,"end_line":230,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Target and lab preflight checks for autonomous loops and auto_pwn.","description":"An autonomous loop that reports success against a target nobody can\nreach is worse than a crash: the operator trusts a finished badge while\nthe gym was down all along. This module answers one question before any\nround is spent — is the target actually up?\n\nTwo liveness sources, cheapest first:\n\n1. Lab membership: when the target IP belongs to a known lab scenario\n   (``modules.lab_runtime.LAB_SCENARIOS``), the authoritative state is\n   the container state itself. A stopped or never-created lab container\n   fails the run before a single command fires, with the exact recovery\n   command in the reason.\n2. TCP reachability: for non-lab targets a bounded parallel probe of\n   common service ports answers whether anything at all listens there.\n\nNever raises; every path returns a mapping. All docker and socket I/O\nis injected so tests run without docker or a network.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["modules/loop_preflight.py::PREFLIGHT_PROBE_PORTS","modules/loop_preflight.py::PREFLIGHT_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_SEC","modules/loop_preflight.py::PREFLIGHT_MAX_WORKERS","modules/loop_preflight.py::NO_PREFLIGHT_HINT","modules/loop_preflight.py::lab_state_for","modules/loop_preflight.py::probe_tcp","modules/loop_preflight.py::check_target","modules/loop_preflight.py::recovery_hint"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
